<title>COLOMBIA: Colombia rebels delay checks of new pipeline blast.</title>
<headline>Colombia rebels delay checks of new pipeline blast.</headline>
<dateline>BOGOTA 1997-07-16</dateline>
<text>
<p>Leftist rebels prevented engineers of the state-run oil company Ecopetrol Wednesday from checking part of the Cano Limon-Covenas pipeline which appears to have suffered a new dynamite attack, a company spokesman said.</p>
<p>The site of the new blast appears to be near the town of El Carmen in northeast Norte de Santander province about 250 miles (400 km) from the site of last week's twin blasts which have paralyzed the pipeline for the last 10 days.</p>
</text>
